<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zeila</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zeila is a port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> coast in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, historically a major outlet for trade between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-highlands">Ethiopian highlands</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> record that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabr-ad-din-iii">Sabr ad-Din III</a> reconstituted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walashma-dynasty">Walashma</a> state at Zeila around 1415. This coastal location placed the new sultanate further from Ethiopian power while securing its trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zeila.jpg" alt="Zeila" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: islamic-art-and-quotes.tumblr.com · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zeila,_Somaliland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
